<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-285] Keep &quot;Pending&quot; when restarting interpreter</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-285</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When some paragraphs have &quot;pending&quot; status and the interpreter gets restarted, the paragraphs persist on &quot;pending&quot; even with the restarted interpreter although they aren&apos;t really pending for execution. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Scenario:&lt;br/&gt;
1. Take an example note where runtime of one of the paragraphs is larger than the time to restart the corresponding interpreter.&lt;br/&gt;
2. Click on &quot;Run all the notes&quot; button to run all the paragraphs. &lt;br/&gt;
3. When the mentioned paragraph with long execution time starts &quot;running&quot;, restart the interpreter. It&apos;ll take a while.&lt;br/&gt;
4. Then refresh the page for your note. You may see that the paragraphs after the paragraph that was executing still have the pending status without real execution. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
